    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": []
    },
    {
      "id": "de99311a-0c90-4c1d-8dac-ae643096b3b6",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left",
        "level": 3,
        "isToggleable": false
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Observation",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "59c99ac5-ad6b-4d83-ac09-97381e911026",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You’ll want to be able to observe and keep notes on how people use what you’ve built. Keep good observational notes that are ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "more",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " than “it seemed people liked it”, and more like, “30% of users used the side filters”. ",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "f74bfc16-db65-42ca-9a41-9e4e2df70894",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Be creepy",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", watch people interact with your product.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": []
    },
    {
      "id": "b1e02c3e-a86f-4e7d-a48c-ec4bec0ed55a",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left",
        "level": 3,
        "isToggleable": false
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Questions",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "dc5d4f9d-74e3-434e-8bea-5524cc095ad2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Ask users questions, verbally or with a form.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "5ad936bf-5abb-421d-8c38-462e8941c56e",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "link",
          "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Likert_scale",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Likert scale",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " questions are often used in surveys (usually these are 5 point scales from strongly disagree to agree). Sometimes you can avoid the middle undecided value and force subjects to either agree or disagree which can be helpful if your subjects are timid. Good Likert questions might look like: “I prefer functionality X over Y”, “Would feature X improve the product”, “logging in is important for this app”. Try to avoid leading questions and have a mix of questions where some you can evaluate numerically and some free form comments.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "fe7b8734-ea94-40cc-a9d3-2f8be7033132",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Don’t ask general questions like “would you use this?”. Ask more specific questions that you want resolved. Do you prefer a slider or a dropdown? How would you use this product? ",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "5f000d38-f091-4997-98d6-3bbdd4c73425",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Avoid asking questions like: ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "“did you enjoy our product / find it useful”",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". These types of questions often suffer from various ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Response_bias",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "response biases",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Survey subjects often suffer from acquiescence bias and try to give you the answer they think you want. So the trick is to construct questions that are balanced and ask for specifics.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "53bb4de5-7804-454d-8845-a4a67fa9082d",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The goal is to inform your further development — what would be useful to know at the start of next term?",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
